tion type to build. Ctrl+Click to add or remove in saved items.Select a collection of bus stations to displaySSelect a lorry station class to display. Ctrl+Click to add or remove in saved itemsPSelect a lorry station type to build. Ctrl+Click to add or remove in saved items0Select a collection of lorry stations to displayMSelect an object class to display. Ctrl+Click to add or remove in saved items¶Select an object type to build. Ctrl+Click to add or remove in saved items. Ctrl+Click+Drag to select the area diagonally. Also press Shift to show cost estimate only)Select a collection of objects to displayISelect a town zone to display. Ctrl+Click to add or remove in saved itemsHSelect a house type to build. Ctrl+Click to add or remove in saved items(Select a collection of houses to displayHouse SelectionÓÅíName: ÓÅÑÓÄ¥ÓÅíPopulation: ÓÅÑÓÄ∑ÓÅíYears: ÓÅÑÓÄ∑-ÓÄ∑ÓÅíYears: ÓÅÑAnyÓÅíYears: ÓÅÑFrom ÓÄ∑ÓÅíYears: ÓÅÑUntil ÓÄ∑ÓÅíSize: ÓÅÑÓÄ∑xÓÄ∑ tilesÓÅíCargo accepted: ÓÅÑÓÄªÓÅíCargo produced: ÓÅÑÓÄõEdge	OutskirtsOuter SuburbsInner SuburbsTown centrePrevent upgradesNChoose whether this house will be protected from replacement as the town growsReplace existing_Choose whether to automatically remove an existing house on the tile where this house is placedDefaultDefault stationDefault road stop	WaypointsDefault waypointÓÅéSignal SelectionÉÓÅíBlock Signal (semaphore)
This is the most basic type of signal, allowing only one train to be in the same block at the same timeèÓÅíEntry Signal (semaphore)
Green as long as there is one or more green exit-signal from the following section of track. Otherwise it shows redêÓÅíExit Signal (semaphore)
Behaves in the same way as a block signal but is necessary to trigger the correct colour on entry & combo pre-signalsêÓÅíCombo Signal (semaphore)
The combo signal simply acts as both an entry and exit signal. This allows you to build large "trees" of pre-signals¿ﬁÓÅíPath Signal (semaphore)
A path signal allows more than one train to enter a signal block at the same time, if the train can reserve a path to a safe stopping point. Standard path signals can be passed from the back side¿ÁÓÅíOne-way Path Signal (semaphore)
A path signal allows more than one train to enter a signal block at the same time, if the train can reserve a path to a safe stopping point. One-way path signals can't be passed from the back sideÇÓÅíBlock Signal (electric)
This is the most basic type of signal, allowing only one train to be in the same block at the same timeéÓÅíEntry Signal (electric)
Green as long as there is one or more green exit-signal from the following section of track. Otherwise it shows redèÓÅíExit Signal (electric)
Behaves in the same way as a block signal but is necessary to trigger the correct colour on entry & combo pre-signalsèÓÅíCombo Signal (electric)
The combo signal simply acts as both an entry and exit signal. This allows you to build large "trees" of pre-signals¿›ÓÅíPath Signal (electric)
A path signal allows more than one train to enter a signal block at the same time, if the train can reserve a path to a safe stopping point. Standard path signals can be passed from the back side¿ÊÓÅíOne-way Path Signal (electric)
A path signal allows more than one train to enter a signal block at the same time, if the train can reserve a path to a safe stopping point. One-way path signals can't be passed from the back side∏ÓÅíSignal Convert
